{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeBoundedJMComm","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeBoundedJMComm","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.HeckeBoundedTransposition"],"declarations":16,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.stdTwoBelow3_jmRaw_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.stdTwoBelow3_jmRaw_comm","kind":"theorem","line":255,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedJMComm.lean#L255-L262","doc":"**`L₁` and `L₂` commute on the 2-dimensional `(2,1)` representation of `H₃(q)`.**\n\nUnreachable from `jmRaw_comm`: `stdTwo_no_stable_extension` proves the unbounded presentation\ncannot host this representation at all. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRaw_comm_of_below","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRaw_comm_of_below","kind":"theorem","line":243,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedJMComm.lean#L243-L247","doc":"Recovers the unbounded `jmRaw_comm` through the downcast. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRawB_comm_adjacent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRawB_comm_adjacent","kind":"theorem","line":238,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedJMComm.lean#L238-L241","doc":"**The adjacent case**, `[L_k, L_{k+1}] = 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRawB_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRawB_comm","kind":"theorem","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedJMComm.lean#L223-L236","doc":"**The multiplicative Jucys–Murphy elements commute** on a bounded presentation.\n\n`Lᵢ L_k = L_k Lᵢ` for all `i, k < n` — the last item of `qou-t1kv`.  Expanding both as `1 + A`, the\ncross terms are `A_i + A_k` on each side and the quadratic term is `addJMB_comm`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRawB_eq_one_add_addJMB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.jmRawB_eq_one_add_addJMB","kind":"theorem","line":210,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedJMComm.lean#L210-L221","doc":"**The two families coincide up to a shift**: `L_k = 1 + A_k` at `d = q − q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.addJMB_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.addJMB_comm","kind":"theorem","line":197,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedJMComm.lean#L197-L206","doc":"**The additive Jucys–Murphy elements commute**, for every `d`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.addJMB_comm_of_le","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.addJMB_comm_of_le","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedJMComm.lean#L183-L195","doc":"**The telescoping step**: `A_i` commutes with `A_{m+1}` whenever `i ≤ m`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.partialSumB_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.partialSumB_succ","kind":"theorem","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedJMComm.lean#L179-L181","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.comm_addJMB_of_comm_sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.comm_addJMB_of_comm_sigma","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedJMComm.lean#L167-L175","doc":"The same lift for `A_i`.  **No bound** — it rides on the relation-free sum expansion. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.comm_transpB_of_comm_sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.comm_transpB_of_comm_sigma","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedJMComm.lean#L139-L165","doc":"If `X` commutes with every `σ_j` for `j < i`, it commutes with `T_(l,i)`.\n\n**No bound**: this is `transpB`'s recursion and the hypothesis, with no relation of `H` used. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_partialSumB_ne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_partialSumB_ne","kind":"theorem","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedJMComm.lean#L127-L135","doc":"**Jucys's centrality property**: `σ_j` commutes with `S_m` for every `j ≠ m`.\n\nTwo bounds, because the two branches constrain different indices. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_partialSumB_above","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_partialSumB_above","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedJMComm.lean#L118-L125","doc":"**Centrality above the cutoff**: for `j > m`, `σ_j` commutes with `S_m`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_partialSumB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_partialSumB","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedJMComm.lean#L93-L116","doc":"**Centrality below the cutoff**: for `j < m`, `σ_j` commutes with `S_m`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.partialSumB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.partialSumB","kind":"def","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedJMComm.lean#L89-L91","doc":"Partial sum `S_m = Σ_{i ≤ m} A_i`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_addJMB_small","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_addJMB_small","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedJMComm.lean#L77-L85","doc":"**3.24(i), the easy direction**: `σ_j` commutes with `A_i` when `i < j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_addJMB","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.Hecke.sigma_comm_addJMB","kind":"theorem","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/HeckeBoundedJMComm.lean#L49-L75","doc":"**Mathas 3.24(i)**, the `i > j+1` case: `σ_j` commutes with `A_i`.\n\nSplit `Σ_{l<i} T_(l,i)` on `l`: below `j` it is `disjoint`, above `j+1` it is `below`, and the two\nmiddle terms commute only **as a pair**. ","signatureChunk":0}]}